{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "All seven completed experiments use singleprofile; the profile-setting dimension (single vs. multi) is entirely unexplored and is a major design axis. The best RNA encoder identified is scvi_n200 (rna_only singleprofile: 0.5203; multimodal singleprofile: 0.5362–0.5399). By testing config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool), I directly compare against config_011 (same encoder, singleprofile, 0.5203) while changing only the profile setting and adding the simplest aggregation (average pooling). This isolates whether multiple profiles with simple averaging add signal over a single profile, without confounding from image modality or fusion. If multiprofile+avgpool improves over 0.5203, it justifies further investment in transformer aggregation and multimodal multiprofile variants; if not, it saves budget by ruling out the profile dimension early. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice given that the profile axis is the largest source of remaining uncertainty."
}

